    "description": "A 5-usable-year study whose first year has negative EPS (sign-crossing EPS CAGR -> unknown), whose TTM EPS sums negative (current P/E and relative value unknown, denominator finding), whose dividends are all zero (average high yield 0, so forecast-low option (d) is NOT selectable -> the whole section 4 degrades to unknown), and whose year-ago quarterly EPS is negative (quarterly change unknown). Every section-9 unknown is asserted as an explicit null and every dependent verdict criterion is unmet_by_insufficiency.",
    "provenance": "Hand-computed 2026-06-11 on paper. Sales and PTP reuse the g01 series (CAGR exactly 10%, margins 12 -> 8% so avg 10, latest 8, declining). EPS = -1.00 then 1.10, 1.21, 1.331, 1.4641: the spec-9 sign rule makes the EPS CAGR unknown, and 2021's negative EPS excludes that year from the P/E and payout averages (remaining four years are constant 20 / 10), and makes ROE 2021 = -1.00 / 5.00 = -20% (within the +/-100 bound, no finding), so average ROE = (-20 + 4 x 20) / 5 = 12 and the latest 20 is 8 pp above -> up trend. All dividends 0: payout and high yield are exactly 0 every usable P/E year, so option (d) divides by a non-positive yield and is not selectable -> forecast low null, zones null, U/D unknown. TTM = -1.00 + 3 x 0.20 = -0.40 (the sum itself is still reported). Average low price = (10 + 11 + 12.1 + 13.31 + 14.641) / 5 = 12.2102. Present yield = 0 / 18 x 100 = 0 exactly; the remaining section-5 outputs are unknown because the projected EPS growth judgment is withheld (null) and the forecast high is unknown. Findings in engine pass order: the 2021 EPS denominator (valuation pass), then the study-level TTM denominator. Normalize-side: the 2021 -> 2022 EPS year-over-year factor is 1.10 / -1.00 = -1.1, which satisfies the break detector's at-or-below-0.67 rule while sales move +10% (not co-moving down), so split_series_break is raised at 2022 on eps - derived from the spec-3 detector rule, the sign-crossing year IS an unexplained series break.",
